ening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-10","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-11','en-b1-11',null,3,11,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-11","baseId":"en-b1-11","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":11,"title":"Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip","objective":"Stop, remember va try bilan -ing/to shaklining ma’noga ta’sirini ko‘rasiz.","context":"O‘quvchi o‘qish paytidagi chalg‘ish va eslab qolish usulini muhokama qiladi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-10"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water.","Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang.","Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang."],"pattern":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","examples":["I stopped checking my phone.","We stopped to drink water.","Remember to save your draft.","I remember meeting her last year.","Try reading the sentence aloud.","He tried to open the locked door."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-11-v0","term":"draft","meaning":"qoralama","ipa":"/drɑːft/","collocation":"save a draft","example":"Remember to save your draft."},{"id":"en-b1-11-v1","term":"aloud","meaning":"ovoz chiqarib","ipa":"/əˈlaʊd/","collocation":"read aloud","example":"Try reading the sentence aloud."},{"id":"en-b1-11-v2","term":"locked","meaning":"qulflangan","ipa":"/lɒkt/","collocation":"a locked door","example":"He tried to open the locked door."},{"id":"en-b1-11-v3","term":"distract","meaning":"chalg‘itmoq","ipa":"/dɪˈstrækt/","collocation":"distract a reader","example":"distract a reader"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"sentence","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","I stopped checking my phone.","We stopped to drink water."]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["O‘quvchi o‘qish paytidagi chalg‘ish va eslab qolish usulini muhokama qiladi.","Remember to save your draft.","Try reading the sentence aloud."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"I remember meeting her last year.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-11-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-11-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"O‘tgan xotira qaysi?","answers":["I remember meeting her."],"explanation":"Remember doing o‘tgan ish xotirasi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["I remember meeting her.","Remember to meet her tomorrow.","I will meet her."]},{"id":"en-b1-11-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Remember ___ save your draft.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["I stopped checking my phone."],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","tokens":["I","stopped","checking","my","phone."]},{"id":"en-b1-11-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I stopped to checking my phone.","answers":["I stopped checking my phone."],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["qoralama","ovoz chiqarib","qulflangan","chalg‘itmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","left":["draft","aloud","locked","distract"],"options":["qoralama","ovoz chiqarib","qulflangan","chalg‘itmoq"]}],"reading":{"title":"Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip — vaziyat","text":"I used to check my phone while doing homework. My teacher suggested stopping this habit for one short study session. I put the phone in another room and tried reading difficult sentences aloud. The change helped me notice missing words. After twenty minutes, I stopped to drink water, then returned to the task. Before closing the editor, I remembered to save my draft. Later I remembered writing one sentence differently, so I compared the two versions. My friend tried to open an old file but could not find it. She had forgotten to save it under a clear name. We learned that a small language difference can describe a different action: stopping a habit is not the same as stopping for a break, and remembering an experience is not the same as remembering to do a necessary job.","sentences":["I used to check my phone while doing homework.","My teacher suggested stopping this habit for one short study session.","I put the phone in another room and tried reading difficult sentences aloud.","The change helped me notice missing words.","After twenty minutes, I stopped to drink water, then returned to the task.","Before closing the editor, I remembered to save my draft.","Later I remembered writing one sentence differently, so I compared the two versions.","My friend tried to open an old file but could not find it.","She had forgotten to save it under a clear name.","We learned that a small language difference can describe a different action: stopping a habit is not the same as stopping for a break, and remembering an experience is not the same as remembering to do a necessary job."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-11-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Stopped to drink water nimani anglatadi?","answers":["paused another task for a drink"],"explanation":"To do yangi maqsadni beradi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["paused another task for a drink","stopped drinking forever","forgot the water"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nima matnni tekshirishga yordam berdi?","answers":["reading aloud"],"explanation":"Reading aloud missing wordsni sezishga yordam berdi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["reading aloud","checking the phone more","closing without saving"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["I used to check my phone while doing homework.","My teacher suggested stopping this habit for one short study session.","I put the phone in another room and tried reading difficult sentences aloud.","The change helped me notice missing words.","After twenty minutes, I stopped to drink water, then returned to the task.","Before closing the editor, I remembered to save my draft.","Later I remembered writing one sentence differently, so I compared the two versions.","My friend tried to open an old file but could not find it.","She had forgotten to save it under a clear name.","We learned that a small language difference can describe a different action: stopping a habit is not the same as stopping for a break, and remembering an experience is not the same as remembering to do a necessary job."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"I stopped checking my phone and tried reading aloud. After twenty minutes, I stopped to drink water. I remembered to save my draft. My friend forgot to save hers and could not find the file later.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-11.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-11-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Qaysi odat to‘xtadi?","answers":["checking the phone"],"explanation":"Stopped checking my phone.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["checking the phone","drinking water","reading aloud"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Do‘stining muammosi nima?","answers":["forgot to save"],"explanation":"Forgot to save.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["forgot to save","saved twice","used a new font"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["reading aloud","twenty minutes"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","rows":["Sinov usuli","Tanaffusdan oldingi vaqt"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["I remember meeting her last year."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-11-dictation.mp3","transcript":"I remember meeting her last year."}]},"writing":{"task":"O‘qishdagi bir muammo, sinagan usulingiz va esdan chiqarmaslik kerak bo‘lgan ishni yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"I had trouble noticing small mistakes in my writing. A teacher suggested trying to read the text aloud. I stopped checking my phone during the exercise and listened to each sentence. After a short time, I stopped to take a break. When I returned, I remembered to save my first draft before editing it. I remember writing one long sentence that was difficult to follow, so I divided it into two. The method did not correct every error, but it helped me focus. Next time I will try asking a friend to explain what they understood before I show them my own plan.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["I stopped checking my phone.","We stopped to drink water.","Remember to save your draft."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bir ma’noli farqni ikki kichik voqea bilan tushuntiring.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"O‘qishdagi bir muammo, sinagan usulingiz va esdan chiqarmaslik kerak bo‘lgan ishni yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-11-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I stopped ___ my phone. (check)","answers":["checking"],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We stopped ___ drink water.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"I remember ___ her. (meet)","answers":["meeting"],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Try doing ko‘pincha nima?","answers":["testing a method"],"explanation":"Yechim usulini sinash.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["testing a method","only a past success","a prohibition"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Avoid bilan qolip?","answers":["avoid using"],"explanation":"Avoid + -ing.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["avoid using","avoid to use","avoid uses"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-11-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["We stopped to drink water."],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","tokens":["We","stopped","to","drink","water."]},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"We stopped ___ drink water.","answers":["to"],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling"},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["I remember meeting her last year."],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","tokens":["I","remember","meeting","her","last","year."]},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Try doing ko‘pincha nima?","answers":["testing a method"],"explanation":"Yechim usulini sinash.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["testing a method","only a past success","a prohibition"]},{"id":"en-b1-11-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["He tried to open the locked door."],"explanation":"Stop doing — o‘sha ishni to‘xtatish. Stop to do — boshqa ishni vaqtincha to‘xtatib yangi ishni qilish: stopped to drink water. Remember to do bajarishni unutmaslik, remember doing esa o‘tgan ish xotirasi. Bir-birini avtomatik almashtirmang. Try to do urinib ko‘rish; try doing yechim sifatida bir usulni sinash bo‘lishi mumkin. Avoid/enjoy + -ing va decide/want + to qoliplarini takrorlang.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","tokens":["He","tried","to","open","the","locked","door."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-11","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-12','en-b1-12',null,3,12,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-12","baseId":"en-b1-12","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":12,"title":"Indirect questions: muloyim ma’lumot so‘rash","objective":"Do you know where …? bilan savolni muloyim va to‘g‘ri tartibda tuzasiz.","context":"Sayyoh axborot stolida yo‘l va jadval so‘raydi.","prerequisites":["en-b1-11"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas.","Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open?","Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y."],"pattern":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","examples":["Could you tell me where the station is?","Do you know what time the train leaves?","I wonder if the museum is open.","Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?","Do you know whether we need to book?","Could you explain how this works?"],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-12-v0","term":"information desk","meaning":"axborot stoli","ipa":"/ˌɪnfəˈmeɪʃən desk/","collocation":"ask at the information desk","example":"At the station, I asked at the information desk rather than guessing where to go."},{"id":"en-b1-12-v1","term":"book","meaning":"oldindan band qilmoq","ipa":"/bʊk/","collocation":"book a ticket","example":"Do you know whether we need to book?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-v2","term":"cost","meaning":"narx turmoq","ipa":"/kɒst/","collocation":"how much it costs","example":"Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-v3","term":"wonder","meaning":"o‘ylamoq, bilgisi kelmoq","ipa":"/ˈwʌndə/","collocation":"I wonder if","example":"I wonder if the museum is open."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"dialogue","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","Could you tell me where the station is?","Do you know what time the train leaves?"]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Sayyoh axborot stolida yo‘l va jadval so‘raydi.","I wonder if the museum is open.","Do you know whether we need to book?"]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-12-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-12-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Indirect yes/no savol qaysi?","answers":["Do you know if it is open?"],"explanation":"If + statement order.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["Do you know if it is open?","Do you know is it open?","Do you know does it open is?"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Do you know where the station ___?","answers":["is"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Could you tell me where the station is?"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","tokens":["Could","you","tell","me","where","the","station","is?"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Could you tell me where is the station?","answers":["Could you tell me where the station is?"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["axborot stoli","oldindan band qilmoq","narx turmoq","o‘ylamoq, bilgisi kelmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","left":["information desk","book","cost","wonder"],"options":["axborot stoli","oldindan band qilmoq","narx turmoq","o‘ylamoq, bilgisi kelmoq"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["information desk","book","cost","wonder"],"options":["ask at the information desk","book a ticket","how much it costs","I wonder if"],"answers":["ask at the information desk","book a ticket","how much it costs","I wonder if"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."},{"id":"en-b1-12-dialogue","type":"dialogue","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Sherik: “Can you give one example?” Siz: darsdagi birinchi namunani qayta tuzing.","answers":["Could you tell me where the station is?"],"tokens":["Could","you","tell","me","where","the","station","is?"],"hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas."},{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Defining relative clauses: Ega relative olmoshi tushishi mumkinmi?","answers":["No, not in “the student who helped”."],"explanation":"Who bu yerda helped ning egasi.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["No, not in “the student who helped”.","Yes, always.","Only if it is a person."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Defining relative clauses"},{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol: Dalilga tayangan xulosani tanlang.","answers":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running."],"explanation":"Must be bu yerda deduction.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running.","You mustn’t enter.","You should rest."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol"},{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip: O‘tgan xotira qaysi?","answers":["I remember meeting her."],"explanation":"Remember doing o‘tgan ish xotirasi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["I remember meeting her.","Remember to meet her tomorrow.","I will meet her."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip"}],"reading":{"title":"Indirect questions: muloyim ma’lumot so‘rash — vaziyat","text":"At the station, I asked at the information desk rather than guessing where to go. “Could you tell me what time the next train leaves?” The assistant said it left at eleven. I then asked how much a return ticket cost and whether I needed to book a seat. She explained that a ticket was available but a seat reservation would help on a busy day. Outside, my friend asked where the museum was. I did not know, so we returned to the desk. The assistant drew a simple route and told us to check the museum’s opening time. Asking a longer question did not make us less clear. It gave the other person a polite way to help while keeping the important question inside. We wrote down the answers and repeated them to confirm the details.","sentences":["At the station, I asked at the information desk rather than guessing where to go.","“Could you tell me what time the next train leaves?","” The assistant said it left at eleven.","I then asked how much a return ticket cost and whether I needed to book a seat.","She explained that a ticket was available but a seat reservation would help on a busy day.","Outside, my friend asked where the museum was.","I did not know, so we returned to the desk.","The assistant drew a simple route and told us to check the museum’s opening time.","Asking a longer question did not make us less clear.","It gave the other person a polite way to help while keeping the important question inside.","We wrote down the answers and repeated them to confirm the details."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-12-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Nega axborot stoliga bordi?","answers":["to ask instead of guessing"],"explanation":"Rather than guessing sabab.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["to ask instead of guessing","to buy a book","to leave luggage forever"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Joy band qilish haqida nima deyiladi?","answers":["helpful on a busy day"],"explanation":"Would help on a busy day, majburiy deyilmagan.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["helpful on a busy day","impossible","always forbidden"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["At the station, I asked at the information desk rather than guessing where to go.","“Could you tell me what time the next train leaves?","” The assistant said it left at eleven.","I then asked how much a return ticket cost and whether I needed to book a seat.","She explained that a ticket was available but a seat reservation would help on a busy day.","Outside, my friend asked where the museum was.","I did not know, so we returned to the desk.","The assistant drew a simple route and told us to check the museum’s opening time.","Asking a longer question did not make us less clear.","It gave the other person a polite way to help while keeping the important question inside.","We wrote down the answers and repeated them to confirm the details."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"Could you tell me what time the next train leaves? It leaves at eleven. Do you know whether I need to book a seat? A reservation is helpful on a busy day. The museum is open until five.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-12.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-12-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Poyezd soati?","answers":["eleven"],"explanation":"Leaves at eleven.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["eleven","five","nine"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Muzey nechagacha?","answers":["five"],"explanation":"Open until five.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["five","eleven","seven"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["eleven","five"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","rows":["Poyezd","Muzey yopilish vaqti"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?"],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-12-dictation.mp3","transcript":"Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?"}]},"writing":{"task":"Safar uchun axborot xodimiga uch savolli odobli email yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"Dear Information Team, I am planning a visit with two classmates next Saturday. Could you tell me what time the first train leaves from our station? I would also like to know how much a return ticket costs for students. Do you know whether we need to book our seats in advance? We hope to visit the museum after arriving, so could you tell me where its nearest entrance is? I have checked the timetable, but I want to confirm the weekend service before buying tickets. Thank you for your help. Best wishes, Lola.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["Could you tell me where the station is?","Do you know what time the train leaves?","I wonder if the museum is open."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Axborot stolida uch muloyim savol bering va javobni qayta tasdiqlang.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Safar uchun axborot xodimiga uch savolli odobli email yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-12-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Do you know ___ it is open?","answers":["if"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Can you tell me how much it ___? (cost)","answers":["costs"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"What time the train ___ (leave)","answers":["leaves"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ichki savolda tartib?","answers":["subject before verb"],"explanation":"The station is.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["subject before verb","verb before subject always","do before every verb"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Whether nimaga xizmat qiladi?","answers":["a yes/no indirect question"],"explanation":"If/whether yes/no ichki savol.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["a yes/no indirect question","only a number","a command"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-12-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Do you know what time the train leaves?"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","tokens":["Do","you","know","what","time","the","train","leaves?"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Can you tell me how much it ___? (cost)","answers":["costs"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?"},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Can you tell me how much a ticket costs?"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","tokens":["Can","you","tell","me","how","much","a","ticket","costs?"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ichki savolda tartib?","answers":["subject before verb"],"explanation":"The station is.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","options":["subject before verb","verb before subject always","do before every verb"]},{"id":"en-b1-12-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Could you explain how this works?"],"explanation":"Indirect questionda ichki qism gap tartibida: Could you tell me where the station is? Is the station emas. Yes/no savollar uchun if/whether: Do you know if the museum is open? Asosiy savolning ohangi va tinish belgisi butun gapga tegishli. Could you tell me …? savol; I wonder … ko‘pincha xabar yoki o‘y.","hint":"Could you tell me where it is? / Do you know if it is open?","tokens":["Could","you","explain","how","this","works?"]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-speak","name":"British Council — Speaking (A1–B2)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2"],"skill":"speaking","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/speaking","task":"Darajangizdagi video vaziyatidan ikki iborani o‘z dialogingizda ishlating.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-b1-12","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Defining relative clauses: Ega relative olmoshi tushishi mumkinmi?","answers":["No, not in “the student who helped”."],"explanation":"Who bu yerda helped ning egasi.","hint":"the student who helped / the book (that) I borrowed / the place where we met","options":["No, not in “the student who helped”.","Yes, always.","Only if it is a person."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Defining relative clauses"},{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol: Dalilga tayangan xulosani tanlang.","answers":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running."],"explanation":"Must be bu yerda deduction.","hint":"must be busy / might arrive late / can’t be here / should ask","options":["She must be busy; her meeting is still running.","You mustn’t enter.","You should rest."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Modals: maslahat, ruxsat va ehtimol"},{"id":"en-b1-12-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip: O‘tgan xotira qaysi?","answers":["I remember meeting her."],"explanation":"Remember doing o‘tgan ish xotirasi.","hint":"stop talking / stop to drink; remember to call / remember calling","options":["I remember meeting her.","Remember to meet her tomorrow.","I will meet her."],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Gerund/infinitive: ma’noni o‘zgartiradigan qolip"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-b1-13','en-b1-13',null,3,13,'published',1,'{"id":"en-b1-13","baseId":"en-b1-13","revision":1,"level":"B1","levelIndex":3,"order":13,"title":"Subject va object questions","objective":"Kim ishni bajarganini va kimga ta’sir qilganini turli savollar bilan so‘raysiz.","context":"Loyiha papkasini kim yuborganini aniqlaysiz.","prerequisites":["en-b1-12"],"minutes":40,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt.","What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping.","Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?"],"pattern":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","examples":["Who sent the file?","Who did you send the file to?","What happened?","What did you find?","Who lives near school?","Which student helped you?"],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-b1-13-v0","term":"send","meaning":"yubormoq","ipa":"/send/","collocation":"send a file","example":"Who did you send the file to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-v1","term":"receive","meaning":"qabul qilmoq","ipa":"/rɪˈsiːv/","collocation":"receive a message","example":"Our group received a file without a clear name."},{"id":"en-b1-13-v2","term":"folder","meaning":"papka","ipa":"/ˈfəʊldə/","collocation":"a shared folder","example":"a shared folder"},{"id":"en-b1-13-v3","term":"happen","meaning":"sodir bo‘lmoq","ipa":"/ˈhæpən/","collocation":"what happened","example":"What happened?"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"sentence","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","Who sent the file?","Who did you send the file to?"]},{"kind":"story","title":"Vaziyatni gapga aylantiring","items":["Loyiha papkasini kim yuborganini aniqlaysiz.","What happened?","Who lives near school?"]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"What did you find?","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-13-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-b1-13-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Qabul qiluvchini so‘raydigan savol?","answers":["Who did you send it to?"],"explanation":"Who obyekt, you ega.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Who did you send it to?","Who sent it?","What happened?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Who ___ near school? (live)","answers":["lives"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Who sent the file?"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","tokens":["Who","sent","the","file?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Who did sent the file?","answers":["Who sent the file?"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["yubormoq","qabul qilmoq","papka","sodir bo‘lmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","left":["send","receive","folder","happen"],"options":["yubormoq","qabul qilmoq","papka","sodir bo‘lmoq"]}],"reading":{"title":"Subject va object questions — vaziyat","text":"Our group received a file without a clear name. The teacher asked, “Who sent it?” Lola said Ali had uploaded it after the meeting. The teacher then asked Ali who he had sent the link to. He had sent it to the whole group, but one classmate could not open it. We checked what had happened and found that the link was private. Ali changed the sharing setting only for our class, not for everyone on the internet. The teacher explained that two similar questions can ask about different roles. “Who sent the file?” asks for the sender. “Who did you send it to?” asks for the receiver. We added a clear title and date, checked the access again, and wrote a short note explaining which version to use.","sentences":["Our group received a file without a clear name.","The teacher asked, “Who sent it?","” Lola said Ali had uploaded it after the meeting.","The teacher then asked Ali who he had sent the link to.","He had sent it to the whole group, but one classmate could not open it.","We checked what had happened and found that the link was private.","Ali changed the sharing setting only for our class, not for everyone on the internet.","The teacher explained that two similar questions can ask about different roles.","“Who sent the file?","” asks for the sender.","“Who did you send it to?","” asks for the receiver.","We added a clear title and date, checked the access again, and wrote a short note explaining which version to use."],"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-13-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Who sent it? nimani so‘raydi?","answers":["the sender"],"explanation":"Who ega: yuboruvchi.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["the sender","the receiver","the date only"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Bir o‘quvchi nega ocholmagan?","answers":["the link was private"],"explanation":"Private sharing sabab.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["the link was private","the file did not exist","all internet was off"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Our group received a file without a clear name.","The teacher asked, “Who sent it?","” Lola said Ali had uploaded it after the meeting.","The teacher then asked Ali who he had sent the link to.","He had sent it to the whole group, but one classmate could not open it.","We checked what had happened and found that the link was private.","Ali changed the sharing setting only for our class, not for everyone on the internet.","The teacher explained that two similar questions can ask about different roles.","“Who sent the file?","” asks for the sender.","“Who did you send it to?","” asks for the receiver.","We added a clear title and date, checked the access again, and wrote a short note explaining which version to use."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Suhbatni tushunish","transcript":"Who sent the file? Ali sent it. Who did he send the link to? He sent it to the whole group. One student couldn’t open it because the link was private. We changed access for the class only.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-13.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-b1-13-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Yuboruvchi kim?","answers":["Ali"],"explanation":"Ali sent it.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Ali","Lola","the teacher"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Kimga ruxsat ochildi?","answers":["the class only"],"explanation":"Class only.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["the class only","all internet users","nobody"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["Ali","whole group"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","rows":["Yuboruvchi","Qabul qiluvchilar"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["What did you find?"],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-b1-13-dictation.mp3","transcript":"What did you find?"}]},"writing":{"task":"Bir loyiha voqeasi haqida yuboruvchi, oluvchi va natijani aniqlaydigan savol-javob yozing.","audience":"Sinfdagi sherigingiz","minWords":90,"maxWords":220,"plan":["Vaziyatni ayting.","Darsdagi til vositasidan foydalaning.","Muhim tafsilot yoki sabab qo‘shing.","O‘qib, ma’no va shaklni tekshiring."],"model":"Our group received a new folder yesterday. Who sent it? Ali uploaded the folder after the meeting. Who did he send the link to? He shared it with our class. What happened when Lola opened it? She could see the photos but not the text file. We checked the settings and found that one document was still private. Ali gave access to the class only, and Lola opened the right version. What did we learn? A clear file name and a simple access check save time, but sharing everything publicly is not a good solution.","modelNotes":["Birinchi gap maqsadni belgilaydi.","Darsdagi tuzilma vaziyatga xizmat qiladi.","Oxirgi gap fikrni yakunlaydi."],"phrases":["Who sent the file?","Who did you send the file to?","What happened?"],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Bir voqeaga ega va obyekt haqida ikkitadan savol bering.","seconds":75,"prompts":["Asosiy fikringiz nima?","Bitta tafsilot yoki misol qo‘shing.","Sherigingizning savoliga javob bering."],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Bir loyiha voqeasi haqida yuboruvchi, oluvchi va natijani aniqlaydigan savol-javob yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-b1-13-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"What ___? (happen, past)","answers":["happened"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Who ___ the file? (send, past)","answers":["sent"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"What did you ___? (find)","answers":["find"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ega savolni tanlang.","answers":["Who helped you?"],"explanation":"Who helped — ega noma’lum.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Who helped you?","Who did you help?","Who did you talk to?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Who does she help? da ega kim?","answers":["she"],"explanation":"Who obyekt, she ega.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["she","who","does"]}],[{"id":"en-b1-13-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Who did you send the file to?"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","tokens":["Who","did","you","send","the","file","to?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Who ___ the file? (send, past)","answers":["sent"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?"},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["What did you find?"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","tokens":["What","did","you","find?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Ega savolni tanlang.","answers":["Who helped you?"],"explanation":"Who helped — ega noma’lum.","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","options":["Who helped you?","Who did you help?","Who did you talk to?"]},{"id":"en-b1-13-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Which student helped you?"],"explanation":"Who called you? — who ega, do/did yordamchisi odatiy tasdiq savolda kerak emas. Who did you call? — you ega, who obyekt. What happened? ega savoli; What did you see? obyekt savoli. Savoldagi noma’lum bo‘lakni avval toping. Ega savolida fe’l mos shaklda qoladi: Who lives here? Obyekt savolda yordamchidan keyin asosiy fe’l: Who does she help?","hint":"Who sent it? ≠ Who did you send it to?","tokens":["Which","student","helped","you?"]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-eur